{
  "name": "Vacancy Outreach | WF3 — Handle Replies",
  "description": "Starts when a new email arrives in Gmail (checked every minute). Labels replies to the outreach emails sent by \"Vacancy Outreach | WF2 — Send And Follow Up\" and updates the lead.",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "acdb82af-5421-5e4b-bc0f-a2a2c40c49b5",
      "name": "Note Read And Label Reply",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        420
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Read And Label Reply\n\nTriggered by: a new email in the Gmail inbox (checked every minute).\n\nWhat it does, step by step:\n1. Reads the Offer and Leads tabs.\n2. Keeps the email only if its thread belongs to a lead that is not stopped, and its Gmail id is not yet in the lead's reply_ids (the Gmail trigger can send the same email twice).\n3. A model labels the reply: interested, not_now, unsubscribe or out_of_office. For interested it also writes a short suggested reply.\n4. Sends the lead to the matching action.\n\nServices called: Gmail (trigger), Google Sheets (Offer, Leads), Venice (model).",
        "height": 630,
        "width": 2420,
        "color": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c8a6de2b-0116-5bd4-956f-2e80febd121f",
      "name": "Note Act On The Reply",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2480,
        420
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Act On The Reply\n\nTriggered by: runs inline after Read And Label Reply.\n\nWhat it does, step by step:\n1. Interested: status replied. The first interested reply from a lead gets a suggested answer in Telegram with three buttons: Approve, Reject, Edit. The run waits up to 24 hours.\n2. Approve sends the suggested answer in the same thread. Reject or no answer sends nothing. Edit opens a form with the answer filled in; Save and send sends the edited answer.\n3. Later interested replies get only a Telegram alert with a link to the thread: the owner answers by hand (CVs, attachments, personal emails).\n4. Unsubscribe: adds the email and domain to the Suppression tab and stops the lead. No email goes there again.\n5. Not now and out of office: status paused (resume by hand in this version).\n6. Every path saves the reply's Gmail id in reply_ids, so a copy sent again is skipped.\n\nServices called: Google Sheets (Leads, Suppression), Telegram (review, alerts), Gmail (reply in thread).",
        "height": 970,
        "width": 2280,
        "color": 2
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "7bd20211-001d-5be1-acf1-b25b1d10fb23",
      "name": "Note Title",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# Vacancy Outreach | WF3 — Handle Replies\n\nReads every new email in the inbox. If it answers one of our outreach emails, a model labels it and the lead is updated. Opt-outs go on the Suppression tab and are never contacted again.\n\n**Starts:** a new email in Gmail (checked every minute). It works with the leads that \"Vacancy Outreach | WF1 — Find And Draft Leads\" saved and \"Vacancy Outreach | WF2 — Send And Follow Up\" sent.\n\n**Sections on this canvas, left to right:** Read And Label Reply, Act On The Reply.\n\n**Labels:** interested (Telegram approval, then the suggested answer is sent), unsubscribe (Suppression tab, lead stopped), not now and out of office (lead paused, resume by hand).\n\n**Services called:** Gmail (trigger, reply in thread), Google Sheets (Offer, Leads, Suppression), Venice (label model, 1 call per reply), Telegram (approval).\n\n**Setup:** see the README next to this workflow file.",
        "height": 360,
        "width": 4800,
        "color": 7
      }
    },
